cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CMP-Agent-Project: Human-in-the-loop closed-loop experimental agent for copper CMP slurry formulation"
abstract: >-
  A domain-specific prototype that couples constrained Bayesian optimization
  (qNEHVI over BoTorch/GPyTorch) with a Pareto-TOPSIS post-processor,
  an experiment ledger with anomaly triage, and a chemical-specific RAG
  microservice for CMP slurry formulation. Not a general-purpose SDK.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "CMP-Agent-Project contributors"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
keywords:
  - chemical mechanical polishing
  - CMP slurry
  - Bayesian optimization
  - multi-objective optimization
  - qNEHVI
  - materials informatics
  - retrieval-augmented generation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Parallel Bayesian Optimization of Multiple Noisy Objectives with Expected Hypervolume Improvement"
    authors: ["Daulton, S.", "Balandat, M.", "Bakshy, E."]
    year: 2021
  - type: article
    title: "BoTorch: A Framework for Efficient Monte-Carlo Bayesian Optimization"
    authors: ["Balandat, M.", "Karrer, B.", "Jiang, D. R.", "Daulton, S.", "Letham, B.", "Wilson, A. G.", "Bakshy, E."]
    year: 2020
